# UndefinedBehaviorSanitizer suppressions
# Suppresses UBSan reports for known intentional patterns in third-party code.
# Loaded via: UBSAN_OPTIONS=suppressions=$PWD/suppressions/ubsan.supp
#
# Format: <check_name>:<file_or_function_pattern>
# Only works for RECOVERABLE checks (must pass -fsanitize-recover=...).
# Check groups like "undefined" can't be used — only fine-grained checks.
#
# IMPORTANT: UBSan rarely produces false positives. Only add entries here
# after confirming the UB is intentional and unavoidable.
